\description{
Generates one row per acute flaccid paralysis (AFP) case, shaped like
the cleaned POLIS case table (\code{polished_afp}) that rise-afg reads.
Non-polio cases arise in each district and year at \code{npafp_rate} per
100,000 children under 15, and \code{n_positive} poliovirus cases are added
in a few districts. Each case carries a date chain that runs in order
from onset through notification, investigation, the two stool
collections, dispatch and arrival at the laboratory, to the culture,
intratypic differentiation (ITD) and headquarters results.
}
\details{
A case whose notification falls after \code{end_date} has not yet been
reported and is left out. Cases are then held pending classification
until their culture result is due, and further cases are made pending,
with recent onsets more likely, until \code{share_pending} of all cases are
pending. A pending case has no result dates and, by default, no age, as
POLIS records it. Among the pending cases, those whose specimens have not
reached the laboratory are classified \verb{LAB PENDING}. Stool adequacy is
derived from the dates and conditions that result, with \code{share_adequate}
of cases drawn to meet the standard.

Column names, the classification vocabulary and the interval columns
follow how rise-afg reads \code{polished_afp} in
\verb{02_scripts/00_helper_functions/0i_pending_helpers.R},
\verb{0j_spi_helpers.R}, \verb{0zb_specimen_helpers.R} and \verb{0a_polis_helpers.R},
and in \verb{02_scripts/2c_indicators/2cvi_timeliness.R}, \verb{2ci_detections.R},
\verb{2cxl_detection_surveillance.R}, \verb{2cxxxiii_followup.R} and
\verb{2cxxxvi_es_profiles.R}. The
pending labels match \code{polis_pending_classes} and the surveillance type
matches \code{pending_surveillance_type} in
\verb{02_scripts/00_helper_functions/00_params.R}. The final culture result
vocabulary beyond \verb{Not received in lab}, the sex labels and the
follow-up findings are not fixed by that code and are chosen here.
}
